-- title:
--   Maximal ideal at a crossing is a branch ideal plus one element
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $N_0$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a level-$(N_0,q)$ Deligne–Rapoport model package `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain equipped with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O :$ `DRLevel.R q` $\to O$ whose maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by the image of $q$, and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$. Write $X_O =$ `DRLevel.XO ρO` for the base change of the model to $O$, and let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\ \kappa\ (\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O)\ 0$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\ \kappa\ (\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O)\ 1$ (the two components of the geometric special fibre), and let $x =$ `𝔛.crossingPt ρO toκ n` be its image in $X_O$ under the first projection followed by the component map and the base-change map `DRLevel.bcMap ρO toκ`. Assume that the points $\xi_\infty$ and $\xi_0$ of $X_O$ attached to $\mathfrak X$ both specialise to $x$, witnessed by `hinf` and `hzero`. Then in the local ring $R = \mathcal O_{X_O,x}$ there exist elements $t_1$ and $t_2$ with $\mathfrak m_R = \mathcal B(\mathrm{hinf}) + (t_1)$ and $\mathfrak m_R = \mathcal B(\mathrm{hzero}) + (t_2)$, where for a specialisation $\xi \rightsquigarrow x$ the branch ideal `Scheme.branchIdeal` is the preimage of the maximal ideal of the stalk at $\xi$ under the specialisation map $\mathcal O_{X_O,x} \to \mathcal O_{X_O,\xi}$.
--
--   This expresses the regularity of each of the two branches of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0q)$ over $O$ at a crossing point: modulo the branch ideal, the maximal ideal of the local ring at the crossing becomes principal, so each branch has a discrete valuation ring as local ring there. It feeds the construction of an explicit two-element generating set in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_span_pair_baseGerm_eq_branchIdeal`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_span_pair_baseGerm_eq_branchIdeal), the local description of the model at an ordinary double point of the fibre at $q$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel_exists_maximalIdeal_eq_branchIdeal_sup_span_singleton.lean

